  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ndpi_strncasestr",
    "file": "ndpi/src/lib/ndpi_main.c",
    "description": "The bounded case-insensitive substring helper computes its loop limit as `str1_len - str2_len + 1` using `size_t` without first checking that `str1_len >= str2_len`. When the bounded haystack is shorter than the needle, this subtraction underflows to a huge value, so the loop increments `str1` and performs reads/`strncasecmp` beyond the packet buffer. The crash is reached from HTTP Authorization handling while searching for `Basic` (and potentially `Digest`), but the unsafe length arithmetic is in `ndpi_strncasestr` itself. The helper should return NULL when the bounded haystack length is less than the needle length and use a non-underflowing loop condition.",
    "conditions": "Supply packet bytes that nDPI classifies along the HTTP path and parses as containing an `Authorization: ` header whose trimmed value has fewer than 5 bytes (or whose bounded `strnlen` is otherwise shorter than `Basic`). In this PoV, the mixed-case `AuthorizaTion:   \\r\\n` line passes the case-insensitive header check; parsing sets a non-NULL authorization pointer, then trims the remaining spaces until its length is zero. `check_content_type_and_change_protocol` calls `ndpi_strncasestr(ptr, \"Basic\", 0)`, yielding `str1_len=0` and `str2_len=5`; the unsigned loop bound underflows and the search reads past the fuzzer-owned input allocation."
  },
